# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify-style header config.
# Plan C in case Render's static-site service ever silently adopts this format
# (their render.yaml `path` glob matcher silently ignored /*, /**, and literal
# `/` — only `*.html` and explicit subdir paths fired). Costs nothing if
# unused; takes effect immediately if migrated to Pages or any compatible host.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, max-age=0
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: origin-when-cross-origin

/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, max-age=0
  Service-Worker-Allowed: /
